# 05 - Short and Long Press

## Objective

Create a program using an ESP32 where 

## Components Used

- ESP32
- 2 LEDs
- 2 220 Ω resistors
- Push button
- Breadboard
- Jumper wires

## Concepts

- GPIO Output
- HIGH and LOW states
- pinMode()
- INPUT_PULLUP
- digitalWrite()
- Debouncing Mechanics
- if statements
- variables

## Wiring

- LED Anode → GPIO 23 (through a 220 Ω resistor)
- LED Cathode → GND 
- LED Anode → GPIO 21 (through a 220 Ω resistor)
- LED Cathode → GND 
- Push button pin 1 → GPIO 22
- Push button pin 2 → GND

## Expected Result

When the button is pressed, the LED lights up for 100ms and the buttonCounter will increment by 1. 

## What I Learned

- Serial Communication
- State Change Detection
- Variable states

